            {
                "entry_id": "29b3a840-b5f7-3868-ba56-f8cb6e0c4695",
                "word": "fermion",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "48ebee9c-9a5a-41ef-a371-37e3e5c8b781",
                        "entry_id": "29b3a840-b5f7-3868-ba56-f8cb6e0c4695",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "fermionen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4323c5e2-9051-3c30-8f63-477d98be8b0f",
                        "entry_id": "29b3a840-b5f7-3868-ba56-f8cb6e0c4695",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een elementair deeltje met een halftallige spin [1]"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "deeltjesfysica"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "12e4c1c9-d364-4409-ae47-82f102d386e4",
                                "sense_id": "4323c5e2-9051-3c30-8f63-477d98be8b0f",
                                "text": "Door hun halftallige spin zijn fermionen onderhevig aan het uitsluitingsprincipe van Pauli."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fe5bc99d-262d-4087-ae51-8facc9565f59",
                        "source_entry_id": "29b3a840-b5f7-3868-ba56-f8cb6e0c4695",
                        "source_sense_id": "4323c5e2-9051-3c30-8f63-477d98be8b0f",
                        "target_lang_word": "fermion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fermion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                        "entry_id": "d9575926-5ac5-3db5-9eaa-7afbd23ace7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any elementary or composite particle that has half-integer spin and thus obeys Fermi–Dirac statistics and the Pauli exclusion principle (equivalently, a particle for which the wavefunction of any system of identical such particles changes sign whenever two are swapped); a baryon, a lepton or a quark;"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "particle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a95faa20-9df3-43d3-ad77-5b2c0b5e17c2",
                                                "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                                "text": "The fermions treated by the Standard Model are the (composite) baryons and the (elementary) leptons and quarks."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "22aa7f4d-2c1c-463b-8ed9-8d0bd36f6417",
                                                "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                                "text": "According to the spin–statistics theorem, the wavefunction of a system of identical fermions (particles of half-integer spin) is antisymmetric under the operation of swapping any two particles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5ab4f81-485a-4ee8-b4a3-861d2abc4fad",
                                                "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                                "text": "A remarkable feature of lattice regularization is the appearance of several fermion species per fermion field in the lattice action."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "173fbb01-b354-4bd8-820b-7e56a89cb979",
                                                "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                                "text": "For 2D systems, going beyond first order pertu[r]bative calculations, we show that the second harmonic of the current is strongly suppressed in the case of spinless fermion models but significantly enhanced for the Hubbard model."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "822fa4e9-d590-4e08-878f-7e120cba3ce8",
                                                "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                                "text": "It is not known whether the Higgs mechanism is the true source for the masses of the fundamental fermions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ee9f320-1f49-4cbf-9de0-4df91a5aad48",
                                                "sense_id": "850c1f91-852a-3e2e-8b4a-0298671f7610",
                                                "text": "The snapshots were taken by MIT physicists and are the first images that directly capture the pairing of fermions — a major class of particles that includes electrons, as well as protons, neutrons, and certain types of atoms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b645c89-28bf-3ddb-9373-c9e6cfb011cd",
                                        "entry_id": "d9575926-5ac5-3db5-9eaa-7afbd23ace7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any elementary or composite particle that has half-integer spin and thus obeys Fermi–Dirac statistics and the Pauli exclusion principle (equivalently, a particle for which the wavefunction of any system of identical such particles changes sign whenever two are swapped); a baryon, a lepton or a quark;\\n(slightly more loosely) any such particle or any composite particle composed of fermions.",
                                            "any such particle or any composite particle composed of fermions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "particle"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "27e1764d-5eb3-4447-bfb1-786f5fe84760",
                        "source_entry_id": "29b3a840-b5f7-3868-ba56-f8cb6e0c4695",
                        "source_sense_id": "4323c5e2-9051-3c30-8f63-477d98be8b0f",
                        "target_lang_word": "fermion",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fermion",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a8a2bd23-d91e-3b8e-a143-9c4ff28a8f33",
                                        "entry_id": "0254ba1e-a583-3f5f-beaa-9aa6fde09845",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Particule possédant un spin demi-entier."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "physical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3324fede-ca76-4dbd-9889-c3462de0d175",
                                                "sense_id": "a8a2bd23-d91e-3b8e-a143-9c4ff28a8f33",
                                                "text": "L’électron, le muon, le neutrino et les quarks sont des fermions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f69584a0-8799-4ca4-8afc-d1b96b9ba686",
                                                "sense_id": "a8a2bd23-d91e-3b8e-a143-9c4ff28a8f33",
                                                "text": "Les bosons sont une famille de particules distincte des fermions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "794025c3-384a-4fb0-8a75-91c88339f675",
                                                "sense_id": "a8a2bd23-d91e-3b8e-a143-9c4ff28a8f33",
                                                "text": "Pourquoi de si grosses machines pour déceler de si petites particules, aux noms pour moi enchanteurs — électrons, muons, neutrinos, quarks, fermions, pions, bosons, hypérons ou kaons ?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
